    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Choose Your Refresh Method",
      "Anchor": "choose-your-refresh-method",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Choose Your Refresh Method"
      ],
      "Text": "Important",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Choose Your Refresh Method",
      "Anchor": "choose-your-refresh-method",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Choose Your Refresh Method"
      ],
      "Text": "Critical: Regardless of how you detect data changes (polling via /validationStatus or push notifications), you must call the actual endpoints (/verificationReport and /identityMe) with the member\u0027s 3-legged OAuth access token to retrieve updated data. Status checks and notifications only indicate that changes exist\u2014they don\u0027t contain the actual data.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Choose Your Refresh Method",
      "Anchor": "choose-your-refresh-method",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Choose Your Refresh Method"
      ],
      "Text": "Use the optional verifiedWithinDays query parameter on /verificationReport for interactive, on-demand freshness checks during member sign-in or other user-driven flows.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "When to Use",
      "Anchor": "when-to-use",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 1: Validation Status API (Polling)",
        "When to Use"
      ],
      "Text": "Performing bulk validation checks (up to 500 members)\nRunning scheduled background jobs\nChecking if member data has been updated without member interaction\nMonitoring validation status across your entire user base",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How It Works",
      "Anchor": "how-it-works",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 1: Validation Status API (Polling)",
        "How It Works"
      ],
      "Text": "Check status (2-legged OAuth, no member consent needed):\n\nCall /validationStatus with up to 500 member ids\nGet status: VALID, INVALID, or VALID_WITH_UPDATES\n\n\nRefresh data (3-legged OAuth, member consent required):\n\nFor members with VALID_WITH_UPDATES or INVALID status\nCall /verificationReport and /identityMe with member\u0027s access token\nStore updated data",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How It Works",
      "Anchor": "how-it-works",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 1: Validation Status API (Polling)",
        "How It Works"
      ],
      "Text": "Tip",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How It Works",
      "Anchor": "how-it-works",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 1: Validation Status API (Polling)",
        "How It Works"
      ],
      "Text": "Make sure you\u0027ve stored the required fields listed in Critical Fields to Persist before implementing this method.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Recommended Polling Interval",
      "Anchor": "recommended-polling-interval",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 1: Validation Status API (Polling)",
        "Recommended Polling Interval"
      ],
      "Text": "Poll once per day (every 24 hours)",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Recommended Polling Interval",
      "Anchor": "recommended-polling-interval",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 1: Validation Status API (Polling)",
        "Recommended Polling Interval"
      ],
      "Text": "Run during off-peak hours to minimize impact\nBatch requests (up to 500 members per call) to stay within rate limits\nOnly call actual endpoints /verificationReport and /identityMe for members with status changes",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Best Practices",
      "Anchor": "best-practices",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 1: Validation Status API (Polling)",
        "Best Practices"
      ],
      "Text": "\u2705 Run polling during off-peak hours\n\u2705 Batch requests (up to 500 members per call)\n\u2705 Only call actual endpoints for members with VALID_WITH_UPDATES or INVALID\n\u2705 Implement exponential backoff for rate limit errors",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Method 2: Push Notifications",
      "Anchor": "method-2-push-notifications",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications"
      ],
      "Text": "Push notifications provide real-time updates when member data changes, eliminating the need for constant polling.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Method 2: Push Notifications",
      "Anchor": "method-2-push-notifications",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications"
      ],
      "Text": "Note",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Method 2: Push Notifications",
      "Anchor": "method-2-push-notifications",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications"
      ],
      "Text": "To set up webhooks and enable push notifications for your application, please work with the Verified on LinkedIn Support team (voli-support@linkedin.com).",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "When to Use",
      "Anchor": "when-to-use-1",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "When to Use"
      ],
      "Text": "You need immediate notification when member data changes\nEvent-driven architecture where you want to react to changes as they occur\nReducing API calls compared to frequent polling",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How It Works",
      "Anchor": "how-it-works-1",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How It Works"
      ],
      "Text": "Register a webhook to receive push notifications\nReceive notifications when member verification or profile data changes\nRefresh data by calling /verificationReport and /identityMe with the member\u0027s 3-legged OAuth access token",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How It Works",
      "Anchor": "how-it-works-1",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How It Works"
      ],
      "Text": "Important",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How It Works",
      "Anchor": "how-it-works-1",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How It Works"
      ],
      "Text": "Push notifications indicate that changes exist\u2014they do not contain the actual updated data. You must call the actual endpoints to retrieve the new data.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How to Register a Webhook?",
      "Anchor": "how-to-register-a-webhook",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?"
      ],
      "Text": "Webhooks allow your application to receive real-time HTTP notifications when subscribed events occur. Only applications with approved webhook use cases can register and receive these notifications. LinkedIn sends notifications only to webhook endpoints that are properly registered and successfully validated.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "1. Register Your Webhook URL",
      "Anchor": "1-register-your-webhook-url",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?",
        "1. Register Your Webhook URL"
      ],
      "Text": "Open your application in the LinkedIn Developer Portal.\nNavigate to the Webhooks tab.\nClick Create Webhook.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "1. Register Your Webhook URL",
      "Anchor": "1-register-your-webhook-url",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?",
        "1. Register Your Webhook URL"
      ],
      "Text": "Note",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "1. Register Your Webhook URL",
      "Anchor": "1-register-your-webhook-url",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?",
        "1. Register Your Webhook URL"
      ],
      "Text": "The Webhooks tab is visible only for applications that have been approved for webhook usage. Applications with the Verified on LinkedIn product will see the Webhooks tab in the Developer Portal. To learn more, refer to our LinkedIn Webhooks Setup guide.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "2. Enter and Test Your Webhook Endpoint",
      "Anchor": "2-enter-and-test-your-webhook-endpoint",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?",
        "2. Enter and Test Your Webhook Endpoint"
      ],
      "Text": "When configuring your webhook in the LinkedIn Developer Portal, enter the HTTPS endpoint where your application will receive LinkedIn push notifications.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "2. Enter and Test Your Webhook Endpoint",
      "Anchor": "2-enter-and-test-your-webhook-endpoint",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?",
        "2. Enter and Test Your Webhook Endpoint"
      ],
      "Text": "Click Test to validate the webhook URL.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "3. Choose Event Types",
      "Anchor": "3-choose-event-types",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?",
        "3. Choose Event Types"
      ],
      "Text": "Select the events your application should be notified about.\nFor Verified on LinkedIn integrations, choose:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "3. Choose Event Types",
      "Anchor": "3-choose-event-types",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?",
        "3. Choose Event Types"
      ],
      "Text": "Notifications of member verification or profile status change.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "3. Choose Event Types",
      "Anchor": "3-choose-event-types",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?",
        "3. Choose Event Types"
      ],
      "Text": "This ensures your webhook receives updates whenever a member\u2019s verification or profile data changes.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "4. Validating the Webhook Endpoint",
      "Anchor": "4-validating-the-webhook-endpoint",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?",
        "4. Validating the Webhook Endpoint"
      ],
      "Text": "LinkedIn validates the ownership of a webhook URL before it can be registered by an application. The validation flow leverages the application\u0027s clientSecret as the secret key along with the universally-known HMACSHA256 algorithm to generate and validate the application\u0027s response to a challenge code.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "4. Validating the Webhook Endpoint",
      "Anchor": "4-validating-the-webhook-endpoint",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Method 2: Push Notifications",
        "How to Register a Webhook?",
        "4. Validating the Webhook Endpoint"
      ],
      "Text": "Once you save the URL and events, the webhook will appear with validation status and notification status along with last validation time.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Event Payload",
      "Anchor": "event-payload",
